{"qid":"Q1028","names":["Morocco"],"title":"Morocco","endonym":{"native":"المملكة المغربية","lang":"ar"},"capsule":"The Alaoui (Alawite) Sultanate was established in 1631 when Moulay al-Sharif founded the dynasty in Tafilalt, and his son Moulay Rashid consolidated control over all Morocco by 1668, ending Saadian rule. Moulay Ismail (r. 1672–1727) centralised power with a slave army (the Abid al-Bukhari), expelled the English from Tangier (1684) and the Spanish from Mahdiya (1681), and built a new imperial capital at Meknes. Morocco retained formal independence through the nineteenth century, resisting French and Spanish encroachment until the 1912 Treaty of Fez imposed a French protectorate; full independence was restored on 2 March 1956. The kingdom remains the world's oldest continuous Alaoui monarchy, represented since 1999 by King Mohammed VI.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Morocco's core territory is historically well documented, but southern boundaries in the pre-colonial Saharan zone were fluid, and the status of Western Sahara remains internationally contested today.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Britannica: Morocco","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Morocco"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Morocco","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Morocco"}],"britannica":"place/Morocco","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Morocco","rulers":[{"qid":"Q303729","name":"Al-Rashid of Morocco","start":1666,"end":1672,"image":"Cherif Muleÿ-Arxid, PA07431.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Cherif%20Mule%C3%BF-Arxid%2C%20PA07431.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"Bertrand, Pierre (French printer, publisher, and print-dealer in Paris, 1600-c. 1678) (artist) (probably publisher)","attributionRequired":false},"nativeName":"الرشيد بن الشريف","nativeLang":"ar"},{"qid":"Q276938","name":"Ismail Ibn Sharif","start":1672,"end":1727,"image":"Ismail Ibn Sharif.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Ismail%20Ibn%20Sharif.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"Germain Moüette","attributionRequired":false},"nativeName":"إسماعيل بن الشريف","nativeLang":"ar"},{"qid":"Q784796","name":"Abdalmalik of Morocco","start":1728,"end":1728,"image":null,"nativeName":"عبد الملك بن إسماعيل","nativeLang":"ar"},{"qid":"Q2827462","name":"Abu'l Abbas Ahmad of Morocco","start":1728,"end":1729,"image":null,"nativeName":"أحمد الذهبي بن إسماعيل","nativeLang":"ar"},{"qid":"Q2836397","name":"Ali of Morocco","start":1734,"end":1736,"image":null,"nativeName":"علي الأعرج بن إسماعيل","nativeLang":"ar"},{"qid":"Q2746037","name":"Abdallah of Morocco","start":1736,"end":1736,"image":"Mouley Abdallah.png","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Mouley%20Abdallah.png?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"Tabyrd6","attributionRequired":false},"nativeName":"عبد الله بن إسماعيل","nativeLang":"ar"},{"qid":"Q2821411","name":"Mohammed II of Morocco","start":1736,"end":1738,"image":null,"nativeName":"مولاي محمد بن إسماعيل","nativeLang":"ar"},{"qid":"Q638863","name":"Zin al-Abidin of Morocco","start":1741,"end":1741,"image":null,"nativeName":"علي زين العابدين بن إسماعيل","nativeLang":"ar"},{"qid":"Q2829253","name":"Al-Mostadi of Morocco","start":1742,"end":1743,"image":null,"nativeName":"المستضيء بن إسماعيل","nativeLang":"ar"},{"qid":"Q548563","name":"Mohammed ben Abdallah","start":1757,"end":1790,"image":null,"nativeName":"محمد الثالث بن عبد الله","nativeLang":"ar"},{"qid":"Q177160","name":"Yazid of Morocco","start":1790,"end":1792,"image":null,"nativeName":"اليزيد 